    SECURITY REVIEW — Creator Income Copilot
    ========================================
    
    Findings (severity / location / status):
    
    1. CSV formula injection in report download — HIGH / static/app.js csvEscape
       Product names (untrusted CSV input) land verbatim in the downloaded report CSV.
       =HYPERLINK(...), +cmd|DDE, @SUM, -2+3 get executed by Excel/Sheets on open.
       FIXED: apostrophe-prefix guard for =,+,-,@,tab,CR (was in tree from pass 1);
       HARDENED this pass: regex widened /^[=+\-@\t\r]/ -> /^\s*[=+\-@]/ so leading-
       whitespace variants (" =cmd|...", tab-prefixed) are neutralized too. Benign
       values stay byte-identical. Parser NOT sanitized deliberately: it emits JSON,
       never CSV; sanitizing would corrupt displayed names (tests pin exact round-trip).
    
    2. XSS via innerHTML — HIGH / static/app.js — NOT VULNERABLE
       Audited all 10 sinks: every API-data interpolation goes through esc()
       (& < > " '). textContent used for subject/body/toast. No eval, no new
       Function, no document.write. Chart labels go to canvas, not HTML. dirBadge/
       severity classes mapped through fixed sets, never raw. Verified live:
       <img src=x onerror=alert(1)> as product name round-trips as data and is
       neutralized at render. CSP (no unsafe-inline/eval for scripts), nosniff,
       XFO DENY, Referrer-Policy no-referrer in place as layer 2.
    
    3. Secrets — HIGH — NOT VULNERABLE
       .env (OPENROUTER_API_KEY) untracked in git, gitignored. /static mount pinned
       to static/ dir; /.env, /static/../.env, encoded traversal all 404 (smoke-
       tested). Key never appears in responses or OpenAPI.
    
    4. File upload / path traversal — MEDIUM — NOT VULNERABLE
       Filename used only for suffix allowlist; content read in-memory, never
       written to disk. store=999/-1/0/abc all 404/422. 5MB cap both paths.
    
    5. SSRF — NONE. Only outbound call: httpx.post to hardcoded openrouter.ai.
    
    6. Unbounded body read before size cap — MEDIUM / main.py — NEW, FIXED this pass
       upload.read() buffered the ENTIRE file and request.json() buffered+parsed the
       whole body before the 5MB check — a 10GB body meant a 10GB RAM allocation.
       Fix: (a) early Content-Length gate (cap + 64KB multipart slack), (b) multipart
       file read in 64KB chunks with running cap, (c) JSON body streamed through
       _read_stream_capped() before json.loads. Residual (documented): chunked-
       encoding multipart without Content-Length still buffered by form().
    
    7. CORS wildcard — LOW informational. 8. PII notes — LOW informational
       (emails never in response; buyer questions flow to OpenRouter by design).
    9. /docs + /openapi.json exposed — LOW informational.
    
